==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|upbringinge}}, equivalent to {{af|en|upbring|-ing|id2=gerund noun}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈʌpˌbrɪŋɪŋ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-upbringing.wav|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[trait]]s [[acquired]] during one's [[childhood]] [[training]]
# The [[raising]] or [[training]] of a [[child]].
#: ''Through her '''upbringing''', Mildred's father had carefully programmed her to expect very little from life.''

